{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_ade2fa10-39f6-43ac-b573-fab4ec9ac9b4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_be904d58b58c4898","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B/20260914T094955Z-aa171c76/runs/specialist/d00cdedfc173451eaf5b312d08e00da9\ncat > $R/specialist_done.partial.json.tmp <<'JSONEOF'\n{\n  \"intent_type\": \"specialist_done\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"confidence\": 0.9,\n    \"domain\": \"enablement_specialist\",\n    \"empty\": false,\n    \"gap_canonical_id\": \"gap.enablement.unknown\",\n    \"new_findings\": [\n      {\n        \"what\": \"BLOCKER 2 (the one behind the attempt-1 runner-type fix) is the benchmark CHILD ENV, not the model. Magpie._build_local_command does env=os.environ.copy() then overlays benchmark.envs verbatim. This pod exports host-physical HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2,3 while Magpie/hyperloom pin ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 for the 2-GPU lease. ROCR filters AND renumbers at the HSA layer, so HIP=2,3 selects nothing: torch.cuda.device_count() still returns 2 but every alloc dies with 'RuntimeError: No CUDA GPUs are available'. Proven by negative control NEG-2 (original script + healthy PATH + HIP=2,3/ROCR=0,1 -> engine-core init failure, rc=1) and by the same command with HIP=0,1 booting fine.\",\n        \"source\": \"reproduced: scratch/gpuprobe (HIP=2,3 FAIL vs HIP=0,1 / unset OK), scratch/neg2/server.log:54 'RuntimeError: No CUDA GPUs are available', Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py:776+800 (env.copy + verbatim overlay), vllm/platforms/rocm.py:128-158 _sync_hip_cuda_env_vars\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Without this the server never initializes: baseline_throughput stays 0.0 and every downstream proposal has nothing to compare against.\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none (env only, no numerical path change)\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"rocm\",\"visible-devices\",\"magpie\",\"enablement\",\"gfx90a\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"what\": \"BLOCKER 3, independent of blocker 2: the session YAML injects PATH=/opt/venv/bin:/usr/local/sbin:...:/bin which does NOT contain the vLLM environment (/opt/envs/vllm/bin). /opt/venv has no vllm, no hf, no transformers, so (a) the InferenceX script's 'setsid vllm serve' dies with 'setsid: failed to execute vllm: No such file or directory' (negative control NEG-1, rc=1 in 28 lines of log) and (b) the bench client's bare python3 (= /opt/venv/bin/python3) cannot import vllm/transformers/huggingface_hub. Magpie was started from /opt/envs/vllm/bin/python3, i.e. the framework env was known at runtime but never propagated to the child.\",\n        \"source\": \"NEG-1: scratch/neg1/out.log:28; probe: env -i PATH=<baseline PATH> -> vllm MISSING, python3=/opt/venv/bin/python3, import vllm -> ModuleNotFoundError; bench client import failure: huggingface_hub ModuleNotFoundError under unpatched PATH vs working --help under patched PATH\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Unblocks both the server phase and the client (throughput) phase; this is the failure that appears immediately after blocker 2 is cleared.\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"path\",\"magpie\",\"inferencex\",\"enablement\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"what\": \"Patch 001 from attempt 1 (gfx90a -> mi300x runner alias) is STILL APPLIED in the live tree (Magpie/modes/benchmark/image_selector.py:139 with an image_selector.py.orig backup), and Magpie._prepare_benchmark_scripts() re-copies Magpie/scripts/benchmark/*.sh over InferenceX/benchmarks/ on every run, so a Magpie-side script edit is the durable place to fix the child env (editing the InferenceX cache copy alone would be overwritten). Script selection is deterministic: benchmarks/gptoss_bf16_mi300x.sh (priority-2 native) does NOT exist, so priority 3 picks the patched Magpie vllm_mi300x.sh.\",\n        \"source\": \"grep gfx90a Magpie/modes/benchmark/image_selector.py:139; Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py:546-570 (_prepare_benchmark_scripts always overwrites), :704-770 (_get_benchmark_script 3-tier priority); ls InferenceX@3d55815/benchmarks/gptoss_bf16_mi300x.sh -> absent\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Tells the next round which layer edits persist, and confirms the reverted attempt-1 patch did not remove the runner alias (so the 'revert' concerned something else / the deeper layers).\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"magpie\",\"patch-propagation\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"what\": \"RUN_EVAL=true is set in the baseline env but lm_eval is NOT installed in /opt/envs/vllm, and InferenceX's _install_lm_eval_deps() pip install is currently failing on this host with network errors (IncompleteRead/BrokenPipe to mirrors.aliyun.com, plus ResolutionImpossible for the 'api' extra on that stale mirror index). vllm_mi300x.sh does 'run_eval ... || exit $?', so an eval-phase failure fails the whole benchmark even when throughput already succeeded.\",\n        \"source\": \"/opt/envs/vllm/bin/python3 -c 'import lm_eval' -> ModuleNotFoundError; /tmp/lmeval*.log; Magpie/scripts/benchmark/vllm_mi300x.sh:148-158 + InferenceX benchmarks/benchmark_lib.sh:870-887,1767-1783\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Risk flag for the Coordinator's end-to-end gate: if the bench succeeds but eval fails, the run is still marked failed. A reachable PyPI index (or pre-installed lm-eval) is needed.\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none for throughput; blocks the accuracy floor measurement\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"lm-eval\",\"eval\",\"network\",\"magpie\"]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"patches_written\": [\"patches/003_rocm_visible_devices_logical_repin.patch\"],\n    \"proposal_set\": [],\n    \"residual_questions\": [\"Is the eval (gsm8k via lm-eval) part of the runnability gate for this round? If yes, a working pip index or a preinstalled lm-eval is required — this host cannot currently install it (mirror flakiness + ResolutionImpossible for lm-eval[api]).\"],\n    \"summary\": \"Attempt-2 DIFFERENT approach, and it reached a fully runnable combo. The runner-type alias from attempt 1 is still live, so the real launch failure was two layers deeper, both in Magpie's benchmark CHILD ENV: (B2) host-physical HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2,3 vs the ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 lease — ROCR renumbers at HSA, so HIP filters everything out -> 'RuntimeError: No CUDA GPUs are available' (NEG-2 reproduced); (B3) the session PATH (/opt/venv/bin, no vllm/hf/transformers) -> 'setsid: failed to execute vllm: No such file or directory' (NEG-1 reproduced). Patch 003 repairs both at the single choke point every local phase flows through (new align_rocm_visible_devices + ensure_framework_env_on_path called from _build_local_command) and hardens Magpie/scripts/benchmark/vllm_mi300x.sh, which previously only repinned HIP when it was UNSET and so could not repair an already-set physical id. VERIFIED: with the patched child env, real TP2/EP vLLM 0.28 server on 2x MI250X booted (Resolved architecture Qwen3_5MoeForConditionalGeneration, CUDA graphs captured, /health 200) and produced correct text ('The capital of France is' -> ' Paris.', 16 tok, 2.3s). Full E2E (server+bench_serving) running now; result in final payload.\"\n  }\n}\nJSONEOF\nmv $R/specialist_done.partial.json.tmp $R/specialist_done.partial.json && python3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('$R/specialist_done.partial.json'));print('partial OK')\"; printf '{\"ts\": \"%s\", \"status\": \"running\", \"note\": \"patch 003 validated: server boots + generates; E2E bench running\"}' \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" > $R/heartbeat.json","description":"Checkpoint partial with findings"}}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f181082-ed15-418f-a6d5-f6b9b40a6948","uuid":"a4d1378f-c3e5-4bc6-afd1-c7f5488611fb"}
