{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_873c59ca6091369d","type":"tool_result","content":"--- gpu:\nGPU[0]\t\t: VRAM Total Used Memory (B): 11042816\nGPU[1]\t\t: VRAM Total Used Memory (B): 11042816\ndiff --git a/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py b/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py\nindex 6b44089..18fd992 100644\n--- a/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py\n+++ b/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py\n@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ import os\n import signal\n import shutil\n import subprocess\n+import sys\n import tempfile\n import time\n import uuid\n@@ -56,6 +57,133 @@ MAGPIE_BUILTIN_SCRIPTS = frozenset(\n     }\n )\n \n+# Device-selection env vars understood by the ROCm/CUDA stacks.\n+_VISIBLE_DEVICE_VARS = (\"HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\", \"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\")\n+\n+\n+def align_rocm_visible_devices(env: Dict[str, str]) -> Dict[str, str]:\n+    \"\"\"Make ``HIP``/``CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` logical indices of the ROCR set.\n+\n+    ``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` filters at the HSA layer and *renumbers* the\n+    agents that survive, so the devices that appear as HIP ids ``0..N-1`` are\n+    the same physical GPUs that appear as ROCR ids ``0..N-1``. Any\n+    ``HIP``/``CUDA`` id taken from a *host-physical* enumeration is therefore\n+    meaningless once ``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` is set: HIP filters the already\n+    remapped ROCR list and, when no id survives, the process ends up with zero\n+    usable devices (``torch.cuda.device_count()`` may still report the ROCR\n+    count while every allocation fails with \"No CUDA GPUs are available\").\n+\n+    A launcher (e.g. a container entrypoint pinning a pod's cards) commonly\n+    exports host-physical ``HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` while Magpie's\n+    ``gpu_selection`` pins ``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` for the benchmark. Merge\n+    the two here, at the single choke point every local benchmark/server phase\n+    passes through, so the child sees a self-consistent set:\n+\n+    * ``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` selects ``N >= 1`` devices -> the request is\n+      satisfiable, so re-pin ``HIP``/``CUDA`` to the logical range ``0..N-1``.\n+    * otherwise, or when the HIP set is already a subset of the ROCR logical\n+      range -> leave the environment untouched.\n+\n+    An explicit ``benchmark.envs.HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES``/\n+    ``CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` in the config counts as a request that the caller\n+    resolved themselves and is only rewritten when it cannot be satisfied.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        env: Environment mapping to mutate in place.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        The same ``env`` mapping (so callers can use either style).\n+    \"\"\"\n+    rocr_raw = (env.get(\"ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES\") or \"\").strip()\n+    if not rocr_raw:\n+        return env\n+    rocr_ids = [t.strip() for t in rocr_raw.split(\",\") if t.strip()]\n+    if not rocr_ids:\n+        return env\n+    rocr_count = len(rocr_ids)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f181082-ed15-418f-a6d5-f6b9b40a6948","uuid":"200e9b9e-b372-44c8-aec5-93b58e789f92","timestamp":"2026-09-14T11:46:21.038Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"--- gpu:\nGPU[0]\t\t: VRAM Total Used Memory (B): 11042816\nGPU[1]\t\t: VRAM Total Used Memory (B): 11042816\ndiff --git a/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py b/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py\nindex 6b44089..18fd992 100644\n--- a/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py\n+++ b/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py\n@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ import os\n import signal\n import shutil\n import subprocess\n+import sys\n import tempfile\n import time\n import uuid\n@@ -56,6 +57,133 @@ MAGPIE_BUILTIN_SCRIPTS = frozenset(\n     }\n )\n \n+# Device-selection env vars understood by the ROCm/CUDA stacks.\n+_VISIBLE_DEVICE_VARS = (\"HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\", \"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\")\n+\n+\n+def align_rocm_visible_devices(env: Dict[str, str]) -> Dict[str, str]:\n+    \"\"\"Make ``HIP``/``CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` logical indices of the ROCR set.\n+\n+    ``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` filters at the HSA layer and *renumbers* the\n+    agents that survive, so the devices that appear as HIP ids ``0..N-1`` are\n+    the same physical GPUs that appear as ROCR ids ``0..N-1``. Any\n+    ``HIP``/``CUDA`` id taken from a *host-physical* enumeration is therefore\n+    meaningless once ``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` is set: HIP filters the already\n+    remapped ROCR list and, when no id survives, the process ends up with zero\n+    usable devices (``torch.cuda.device_count()`` may still report the ROCR\n+    count while every allocation fails with \"No CUDA GPUs are available\").\n+\n+    A launcher (e.g. a container entrypoint pinning a pod's cards) commonly\n+    exports host-physical ``HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` while Magpie's\n+    ``gpu_selection`` pins ``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` for the benchmark. Merge\n+    the two here, at the single choke point every local benchmark/server phase\n+    passes through, so the child sees a self-consistent set:\n+\n+    * ``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` selects ``N >= 1`` devices -> the request is\n+      satisfiable, so re-pin ``HIP``/``CUDA`` to the logical range ``0..N-1``.\n+    * otherwise, or when the HIP set is already a subset of the ROCR logical\n+      range -> leave the environment untouched.\n+\n+    An explicit ``benchmark.envs.HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES``/\n+    ``CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` in the config counts as a request that the caller\n+    resolved themselves and is only rewritten when it cannot be satisfied.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        env: Environment mapping to mutate in place.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        The same ``env`` mapping (so callers can use either style).\n+    \"\"\"\n+    rocr_raw = (env.get(\"ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES\") or \"\").strip()\n+    if not rocr_raw:\n+        return env\n+    rocr_ids = [t.strip() for t in rocr_raw.split(\",\") if t.strip()]\n+    if not rocr_ids:\n+        return env\n+    rocr_count = len(rocr_ids)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
