{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_cea09f14-0c72-4468-98d0-0b92e7deae6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nDone. Final `specialist_done.json` is written and validated.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Root cause (attempt 2, different layer than the reverted attempt):** the model is *not* the problem — `Qwen3_5MoeForConditionalGeneration` is natively supported by vLLM 0.28.0+rocm723 and resolves at runtime. Attempt 1's `gfx90a→mi300x` runner alias is still live in the tree, so the real launch failure sat **two layers deeper, in Magpie's benchmark child env**:\n\n| # | Blocker | Proof (negative control, original scripts) |\n|---|---|---|\n| B2 | Pod exports host-physical `HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2,3` while the lease pins `ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1`. ROCR filters **and renumbers** at the HSA layer, so HIP selects nothing → `RuntimeError: No CUDA GPUs are available` → \"Engine core initialization failed\" | `scratch/neg2` rc=1 with a *healthy* PATH |\n| B3 | Injected `PATH=/opt/venv/bin:…` has no `vllm`/`hf`/`transformers` | `scratch/neg1`: `setsid: failed to execute vllm: No such file or directory` in ~2 s |\n\n**Deliverable:** `patches/003_rocm_visible_devices_logical_repin.patch` — adds `align_rocm_visible_devices()` + `ensure_framework_env_on_path()` at `_build_local_command` (the single funnel every local server/client phase flows through), and hardens `Magpie/scripts/benchmark/vllm_mi300x.sh`, whose existing logic only repinned HIP **when HIP was unset** and so could never repair an already-set physical id. `git apply --check` passes against the live tree; it is not applied (integrates via `integrate_patch`). No `proposal_set` padding, no setup commands.\n\n**Verified runnable on my leased cards:** TP2 + EP server booted, CUDA graphs captured, `/health` 200, correct generation (`\"The capital of France is\"→\" Paris.\"`), and a **full Magpie/InferenceX `benchmark_serving` run completed: 64/64 requests, 1151.77 tok/s output, TTFT 4358.9 ms, TPOT 50.3 ms** (my validation numbers, not the sealed baseline).\n\n**Next (deeper) failure, honest:** only the *eval* stage — `RUN_EVAL=true` but `lm_eval` isn't installed and pip fails to both mirrors.aliyun.com and pypi.org with connection resets (`lm-eval[api]` also hits `ResolutionImpossible` on the stale mirror). InferenceX self-installs it, so a reachable index is the only requirement; the throughput gate is unaffected. GPUs left clean, no processes of mine running."}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f181082-ed15-418f-a6d5-f6b9b40a6948","uuid":"886cae00-1b4d-47b6-8801-d2a94e20adb6"}
